From: opencreator-os
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: ingenic: keep a watchdog that is already running fed

chainload.ko arms the watchdog right before it jumps into this kernel, so
a test kernel that hangs resets the SoC. The SDK probe neither stops nor
reports a running counter, so nothing fed it until procd opens
/dev/watchdog. Set WDOG_HW_RUNNING when the counter is enabled at probe:
with CONFIG_WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED the watchdog core then pings it
(every timeout / 2) until userspace takes over. A normal boot is
unchanged: the SPL leaves the counter disabled.

--- a/module_drivers/drivers/watchdog/ingenic_wdt.c
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/watchdog/ingenic_wdt.c
@@ -286,6 +286,13 @@ static int ingenic_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	clk_prepare_enable(drvdata->wdt_clk);
 	clk_prepare_enable(drvdata->tcu_clk);
 
+	/* Armed before this kernel started (chainload.ko arms it for a test
+	 * boot; the SPL leaves it off): mark it running so the watchdog core
+	 * feeds it until userspace opens /dev/watchdog
+	 * (CONFIG_WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED). */
+	if (readb(drvdata->base + INGENIC_REG_WDT_COUNTER_ENABLE) & 0x1)
+		set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &ingenic_wdt->status);
+
 	ret = watchdog_register_device(&drvdata->wdt);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		goto err_disable_clk;
